in @prism
in @meta
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/reality

# @epistemologic/reality/silicon — the running CPU + memory family root.
#
# Silicon is the species of reality the substrate has been carrying
# longest. It names what the observer sees when they look at the
# running machine's hardware: ISA, microarchitecture, memory model,
# compute budgets, dependency-flake references. Each carrier under this
# root specializes the literal property (re-detect, content-address,
# compare) at its own slice of the silicon surface.
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
#   @epistemologic/reality/silicon/arch          ISA + microarch carriers.
#                                                arch/arm64 + arch/x86_64.
#   @epistemologic/reality/silicon/memory        memory model, total bytes,
#                                                page size, cache hierarchy.
#   @epistemologic/reality/silicon/compute_bound budget carrier the shard's
#                                                admits-action allocates.
#   @epistemologic/reality/silicon/flake_ref     typed reference to a nix
#                                                flake (URL + locked rev).
#
# Per docs/specs/shard-design.md §2/§4: every silicon carrier is one of
# the four type carriers the @mirror/shard.shard record composes from.
# Fate's |\> tournament reads the carrier set as input to pick the
# locally-optimal Au binary for the running system.
#
# Substrate-pull placement (2026-06-06, Mara's reality family migration):
# moved from shards/epistemologic/silicon/ to shards/epistemologic/reality/silicon/
# per the @epistemologic/reality family declaration; silicon is one
# species of reality. The species root names the carrier set; each
# carrier file under the root specializes.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/shard-design.md (the four type carriers),
#               docs/insights/2026-05-25-pipe-hole-and-au-binary.md
#               (the Fate-tournament input set).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]].
# Related shards: epistemologic/reality.mirror (the family root above),
#                 epistemologic/reality/silicon/arch/{arm64,x86_64}.mirror,
#                 epistemologic/reality/silicon/memory.mirror,
#                 epistemologic/reality/silicon/compute_bound.mirror,
#                 epistemologic/reality/silicon/flake_ref.mirror.
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/epistemologic/reality/silicon.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/reality/silicon` and only that.

out @epistemologic/reality/silicon
